From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] util/mesa_cache_db_multipart: RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY=1 is RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1

T172 integration. t168d's lead-mesh-40 (RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY: ask every
database part before compressing a put, drop a key any part holds) and
lead-mesh-30 (RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN) do the same job. One is kept:
lead-mesh-30's, because it also
- makes the room check and the write one step under the part's lock (writers
  racing near a part's cap no longer compact it; a full part is passed over),
- looks a key up again under the lock before writing (a key written by another
  thread since the first look is not written twice),
- remembers absent parts (a miss no longer stats every absent part's folder),
- covers the multi-file cache too (one access() before compressing).
t168d's lead-mesh-40 asked only parts that were open (it opened the existing
ones once) and only exclusive caches; its count (skipped=, skipped_mib=) is the
RADV_PS5_CACHE line's known= / known_mib= (lead-mesh-34 as rebased).

So this only makes RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY=1 (exactly "1") switch on the
same code as RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1; either name, or both, gives the
same behaviour. The stderr line says which name turned it on. Nothing about
keys, entries, files or the cache UUID changes. Ours.

Compiled with the driver's flags, syntax only. Not linked, not run on the console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5
---
diff --git a/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.c b/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.c
index 68053c7..04e46d0 100644
--- a/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.c
+++ b/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.c
@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@
 #define EXCLUSIVE_DEFAULT false
 #endif
 
-/* EglantinePS5: RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1 (exactly "1", read once per process; off
- * otherwise). Upstream writes every put it is handed, and compresses it first (zlib at level 9
+/* EglantinePS5: RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1, or its alias RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY=1
+ * (exactly "1", read once per process; off otherwise). Upstream writes every put it is handed, and compresses it first (zlib at level 9
  * on the PS5 build, which has no zstd): the multi-file cache then evicts for room before it
  * finds that the file is there already, and the database looks only in the part it writes to,
  * after making room, so a key held by another part is stored again. With the switch:
@@ -49,9 +49,15 @@ mesa_cache_db_multipart_skip_known(void)
    int on = p_atomic_read(&multipart_skip_known);
    if (on < 0) {
       const char *value = getenv("RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN");
-      on = value && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0';
+      /* lead-mesh-40 (T172): RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY=1 is the same switch (t168d's
+       * lead-mesh-40 asked every part before compressing too; this implementation is kept). */
+      const char *alias = getenv("RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY");
+      const bool by_name = value && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0';
+      const bool by_alias = alias && alias[0] == '1' && alias[1] == '\0';
+      on = by_name || by_alias;
       if (p_atomic_cmpxchg(&multipart_skip_known, -1, on) == -1 && on)
-         fprintf(stderr, "RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1 on\n");
+         fprintf(stderr, "RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1 on%s\n",
+                 by_name ? "" : " (as RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY=1)");
    }
    return on != 0;
 }
diff --git a/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.h b/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.h
index 9ec0c65..39e00e4 100644
--- a/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.h
+++ b/src/util/mesa_cache_db_multipart.h
@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@ struct mesa_cache_db_multipart {
    bool fast;
 };
 
-/* EglantinePS5: RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1 (exactly "1", read once per process). */
+/* EglantinePS5: RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_SKIP_KNOWN=1 or RADV_PS5_DISK_CACHE_ONE_COPY=1 (exactly "1",
+ * read once per process). */
 bool
 mesa_cache_db_multipart_skip_known(void);
 
